## Off-limits (must not be modified)

- <PATH_TO_SOURCE_ROOT> (the source tree — **its content must not be changed**. Work on the
  modernized tree instead)
- **Only three git operations are permitted**: `git init` / the initial commit / adding a `.gitignore`
  (because ATX requires git management)
  - Forbidden: adding a remote / push / reset / rebase / deleting branches / force operations
  - If the source tree is a git repository: do not push/commit to upstream's protected branches
- **Writes originating from ATX are an exception** (unavoidable tool behaviour): appending to
  `.gitignore`, creating the `atx-result-staging-<id>` branch, and `git add .` plus a commit.
  That is exactly why the branch and HEAD are confirmed to match before and after an ATX run
  (Phase 0a-3)
